.TH HD-PLYMOUTH-RENDER 8 "October 2026" "hd-desktop" "HyprDebian"
.SH NAME
hd-plymouth-render \- render the boot splash of HyprDebian in the theme of the system
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hd-plymouth-render
.RB [ \-\-update\-initramfs ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hd-plymouth-render
renders the boot splash of HyprDebian, the
.BR plymouth (8)
theme
.B hyprdebian
of
.BR hd-plymouth (7),
in the theme of the system: the key
.B hd-theme
of
.IR /etc/hyprdebian/config.json ,
which
.B hd-theme \-\-select
sets as root; see
.BR hd-theme (7).
The themes of the users are not used.
A member that is missing or not valid takes the value of the theme
.BR default ,
which is also used when the system has no theme.
.PP
The script of plymouth cannot read the theme at boot, so it is rendered
into the files of the plymouth theme, in
.IR /var/lib/hd-plymouth/theme ,
which
.I /usr/share/plymouth/themes/hyprdebian/hyprdebian.plymouth
names as its
.B ImageDir
and
.BR ScriptFile :
.TP
.I hyprdebian.script
The script, from the jinja2 template in
.IR /usr/share/hd-plymouth/templates ,
with the font of the theme at
.B font-size-normal
in the field and
.B font-size-small
below it, the colour
.B light
for all text and
.B dark
behind the background.
.TP
.IR field-input.png ", " field-check.png ", " field-fail.png
The input field of 650 by 100 pixels, as in hyprlock.conf: the fill in
.B dark
at
.BR opacity ,
with corners of
.BR radius ,
and an outline of
.B border
pixels in
.BR highlight ,
and in the yellow and the red of hyprlock while a password is checked and
after a wrong one.
The inner corners have the radius minus the border.
.TP
.I dot.png
The dot of a typed character, in
.BR light .
.TP
.I background.png
A link to the image of the family
.B background
in
.I /usr/share/backgrounds/hyprdebian
that best fits the largest connected monitor: the smallest that covers it,
else the largest.
Without a connected monitor, it fits a screen of 1920x1080.
.PP
.I /var/lib/hd-plymouth/fonts
lists the files of the fonts of the splash, as
.BR fc-match (1)
finds them.
.PP
A file is only written when it changes.
The hook
.I /usr/share/initramfs-tools/hooks/hd-plymouth
runs
.B hd-plymouth-render
before it puts the splash and its fonts in the initramfs, so every initramfs
has the splash in the theme of the system at that moment.
The installation of hd-desktop runs it too.
.PP
Run it as root.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ,\  \-\-help
Show a short help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-update\-initramfs
When a file changed and plymouth uses the theme
.BR hyprdebian ,
rebuild the initramfs of all kernels with
.BR "update-initramfs \-u \-k all" ;
hd-bootloader then rebuilds its UKIs.
.B hd-theme \-\-select
runs it with this option as root.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when the splash was rendered, and with
.B \-\-update\-initramfs
the initramfs rebuilt when needed; 1 on an error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/hyprdebian/config.json
The theme of the system, in the key
.BR hd-theme .
.TP
.I /usr/share/hd-plymouth/templates/hyprdebian.script.j2
The template of the script.
.TP
.I /var/lib/hd-plymouth/theme
The rendered files of the plymouth theme.
.TP
.I /var/lib/hd-plymouth/fonts
The files of the fonts, for the initramfs.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hd-plymouth (7),
.BR hd-theme (1),
.BR hd-theme (7),
.BR plymouth (8),
.BR update-initramfs (8)
